/-
# Formalizing Statistical Mechanics in Lean 4

Root module: imports the formalized blueprint nodes.  Built bottom-up along the
blueprint dependency graph (`leanblueprint`); every declaration is sorry-free and
uses only Mathlib's foundational axioms.

Phase 0 — measure-theoretic foundations:
* `Code.Foundations.ConfigSpace`          — `def:config-space`
* `Code.Foundations.ProductMeasure`       — `def:product-measure`
* `Code.Foundations.StochasticDomination` — `def:stochastic-domination`
* `Code.Foundations.WeakConvergence`      — `def:weak-convergence`
* `Code.Foundations.Ergodicity`           — `def:ergodicity`
* `Code.Foundations.Kolmogorov`           — `thm:kolmogorov`
* `Code.Foundations.Prokhorov`            — `thm:prokhorov`
* `Code.Foundations.CondDistribution`     — `def:cond-distribution`

Phase 1 — correlation inequalities:
* `Code.Inequalities.IncreasingEvent`     — `def:increasing-event`, `def:fkg-lattice-condition`
* `Code.Inequalities.FKG`                 — `thm:fkg`, `thm:holley`
* `Code.Inequalities.Harris`              — `cor:harris`
* `Code.Inequalities.Pivotal`             — `def:pivotal`
* `Code.Inequalities.DisjointOccurrence`  — `def:disjoint-occurrence`
* `Code.Inequalities.Russo`               — `thm:russo`
* `Code.Inequalities.BK`                  — `thm:bk`
* `Code.Inequalities.OSSS`                — `thm:osss`

Phase 2 — lattice / graph combinatorics:
* `Code.Lattice.HypercubicLattice`        — `def:lattice`
* `Code.Lattice.Clusters`                 — `def:clusters`
* `Code.Lattice.BoundaryConditions`       — `def:boundary-conditions`
* `Code.Lattice.PlanarDual`               — `def:planar-dual`

Phase 3 — random-cluster (FK) model:
* `Code.FK.Potts`                         — `def:potts`
* `Code.FK.RandomCluster`                 — `def:fk-measure`
* `Code.FK.FKG`                           — `thm:fk-fkg`
* `Code.FK.Comparison`                    — `thm:fk-comparison`
* `Code.FK.EdwardsSokal`                  — `thm:edwards-sokal`
* `Code.FK.InfiniteVolume`                — `def:fk-infinite-volume`

Phase 4 — Bernoulli percolation:
* `Code.Percolation.Theta`                — `def:theta`
* `Code.Percolation.TildePc`              — `def:tilde-pc`

Phase 5 — Ising model:
* `Code.Ising.Gibbs`                      — `def:ising-gibbs`
* `Code.Ising.Pressure`                   — `thm:pressure`
* `Code.Ising.GKS`                        — `thm:gks`
* `Code.Ising.InfiniteVolume`             — `def:ising-bc`
-/
